<h2>Proportion: φ, not columns</h2>
<p>The twelve columns do not reach a 1920 × 1080 canvas — there are no columns on a camera. What divides a source inside itself is the <a href="/layout/golden/">golden ratio</a>: the card is a golden rectangle, the camera frame is one too, the ticker’s tag is the minor part of its own bar, and the lamp sits one φ-step from its word.</p>
<p>The ticker’s items are written twice: the track travels half its own width and begins again, so the loop has no seam. <code>--im-studio-ticker-speed</code> is the one pass. The chat’s messages arrive 1.4s apart (<code>im-studio-stagger</code>); <code>data-member</code> marks a member with a star, <code>data-host</code> fills the host’s avatar with the accent. The clock’s <code>[data-im-clock]</code> is kept honest by <code>im.js</code>; the markup carries a time so the frame is right before any script runs.</p>
